From 68ca440a7f70e9992a5508f9c2be2d9aa37dd95e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rolotrealanis98 <122947376+rolotrealanis98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:54:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth panel: AirPods noise control, battery and ear
 detection

Under a connected AirPods row, show battery (left, right, case), ear
detection, the listening mode (Off, Transparency, Adaptive, ANC) and
conversation awareness; m cycles the mode from the keyboard.

AirPods allow a single AAP connection, so the panel does not open one. It
reads state from, and sends commands to, a user service over a Unix socket
at $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/airpods-control.sock (newline-delimited JSON). The
client connects only while the panel is open with an AirPods connected;
without the service, or with any other headset, nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: rolotrealanis98 <122947376+rolotrealanis98@users.noreply.github.com>
